&lt;h2 id=&quot;conclusion&quot;&gt;Conclusion&lt;&#x2F;h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Only use &lt;code&gt;make&lt;&#x2F;code&gt; if you actually need a build system, otherwise use a proper task runner tool. I personally think the convenience is well worth having one extra dependency, and this is a non-issue if the project comes with its environment (e.g. &lt;del&gt;conda&lt;&#x2F;del&gt; &lt;a rel=&quot;noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;mamba.readthedocs.io&#x2F;en&#x2F;latest&#x2F;user_guide&#x2F;micromamba.html&quot;&gt;micromamba&lt;&#x2F;a&gt;, &lt;a rel=&quot;noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.docker.com&#x2F;&quot;&gt;docker&lt;&#x2F;a&gt;, &lt;a rel=&quot;noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;nixos.org&quot;&gt;nix&lt;&#x2F;a&gt;, &lt;a rel=&quot;noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;prefix-dev&#x2F;pixi&quot;&gt;pixi&lt;&#x2F;a&gt;). In any case, reimplementing it with shell script glue is risky and time consuming.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
